  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MIGRATORY BIRD CONSERVATION IN WESTERN PORTLAND BIGHT, JAMAICA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: 1) actively and collaboratively manage the Western Portland Bight Reserve (WPBR) to support migratory bird conservation; 2) improve Caribbean Coastal Area Management Foundations capacity to implement conservation actions in WPBR; 3) survey baseline conditions for NMB populations and habitat and complete a baseline report; 4) develop and implement NMB bird population and habitat monitoring; 5) develop and implement community enforcement, monitoring and conservation actions; 6) promote bird-related tourism as a source of support and sustainable livelihoods; 7) operationalize the visitor center to support education, enforcement, and community-based ecotourism; and 8) increase awareness and support for WPBR management by providing educational programs for resident adults and children.</narrative>
  </description>
